---
/*
  The navy band. In Figma the rectangle is 900px wide on an 800px frame and sits at
  y=-35 -- it overhangs both edges, which reads as "this band runs edge to edge".
  So the band is full-bleed and only its contents are capped at the content column.

  The phone frame breaks the wordmark after "Camargo" and gives the band two lines.
  Left to itself the text would instead squeeze onto one line that touches both
  margins, so below `sm` each half is its own block; from `sm` up they are inline
  again and the line breaks (or doesn't) wherever the width allows.
*/
---
<header class="w-full bg-navy">
  <div
    class="mx-auto flex min-h-masthead max-w-column items-center justify-center px-gutter"
  >
    <h1
      class="m-0 pb-mark-lift text-center font-display text-mark font-medium leading-tight text-cream/80"
    >
      <span class="block sm:inline">Igor de Camargo</span>{' '}<span
        class="block sm:inline">e Souza Câmara</span
      >
    </h1>
  </div>
</header>
